      "body": "### The problem\r\n\r\nI noticed that my IKEA motion sensors don't work anymore (automations don't trigger since there is no state change) in the latest beta.\r\n\r\nWhen I trigger the motion sensor I see the following error messages relating to zigpy/zha:\r\n```\r\n2023-03-31 19:45:49.749 WARNING (MainThread) [zigpy.util] Error calling listener <bound method OnOffChannel.cluster_command of <homeassistant.components.zha.core.channels.general.OnOffChannel object at 0x7f3308523fd0>> with args (4, 66, on_with_timed_off(on_off_control=<OnOffControl: 0>, on_time=1800, off_wait_time=0)): TypeError(\"'ZCLCommandDef' object is not subscriptable\")\r\n2023-03-31 19:45:50.360 WARNING (MainThread) [bellows.thread] Attempted to use a closed event loop\r\n2023-03-31 19:45:55.363 ERROR (MainThread) [homeassistant] Error doing job: Task exception was never retrieved\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/jurriaan/.pyenv/versions/3.11.2/lib/python3.11/asyncio/tasks.py\", line 490, in wait_for\r\n    return fut.result()\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nasyncio.exceptions.CancelledError\r\n\r\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/jurriaan/homeassistant/lib/python3.11/site-packages/bellows/ezsp/v9/__init__.py\", line 51, in pre_permit\r\n    await self.setPolicy(\r\n  File \"/home/jurriaan/.pyenv/versions/3.11.2/lib/python3.11/asyncio/tasks.py\", line 492, in wait_for\r\n    raise exceptions.TimeoutError() from exc\r\nTimeoutError\r\n2023-03-31 19:46:51.052 WARNING (MainThread) [zigpy.util] Error calling listener <bound method OnOffChannel.cluster_command of <homeassistant.components.zha.core.channels.general.OnOffChannel object at 0x7f3266c35490>> with args (88, 66, on_with_timed_off(on_off_control=<OnOffControl: 0>, on_time=1800, off_wait_time=0)): TypeError(\"'ZCLCommandDef' object is not subscriptable\")\r\n2023-03-31 19:47:11.800 WARNING (MainThread) [zigpy.util] Error calling listener <bound method OnOffChannel.cluster_command of <homeassistant.components.zha.core.channels.general.OnOffChannel object at 0x7f3266d6b790>> with args (65, 66, on_with_timed_off(on_off_control=<OnOffControl: 0>, on_time=1800, off_wait_time=0)): TypeError(\"'ZCLCommandDef' object is not subscriptable\")\r\n2023-03-31 19:47:24.095 WARNING (MainThread) [zigpy.appdb] Discarding _save_attribute event\r\n2023-03-31 19:47:28.358 WARNING (MainThread) [zigpy.util] Error calling listener <bound method OnOffChannel.cluster_command of <homeassistant.components.zha.core.channels.general.OnOffChannel object at 0x7f3308523fd0>> with args (6, 66, on_with_timed_off(on_off_control=<OnOffControl: 0>, on_time=1800, off_wait_time=0)): TypeError(\"'ZCLCommandDef' object is not subscriptable\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What version of Home Assistant Core has the issue?\r\n\r\ncore-2023.4.0b2\r\n\r\n### What was the last working version of Home Assistant Core?\r\n\r\nIt worked fine on 2023.3 before I upgraded to the beta.\r\n\r\n### What type of installation are you running?\r\n\r\nHome Assistant Core\r\n\r\n### Integration causing the issue\r\n\r\nzha\r\n\r\n### Link to integration documentation on our website\r\n\r\nhttps://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/zha/\r\n\r\n### Diagnostics information\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Example YAML snippet\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Anything in the logs that might be useful for us?\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\n_No response_",
